 To find the answer, let's start by establishing the ratio of chocolate chips to cookies as follows:
\begin{align}
&\text{ $8$ cups of chocolate chips to $12$ cookies}\\
&\Rightarrow \text{ 1 cup of chocolate chips to $\dfrac{12}{8}$ cookies }\\
