Now, let's calculate how many cups of chocolate chips are needed for $15$ cookies.
\begin{align}
& 1\text{ cup of chocolate chips to }\dfrac{12}{8}\text{ cookies}\\
& 15\text{ cups of chocolate chips to }\dfrac{12}{8}\times 15\text{ cookies}\\
