We start by initializing our dynamic programming table dp with zeros. We then fill in the table using the following recurrence relation:

dp[i][j] = dp[i][j+1] + dp[i-n[j]][j+1]

Here, dij is the maximum number of cupcakes of color j that can be taken, and N is the total number of cupcakes. If dij = 0, then it is not possible to take any cupcakes of color j, so dp[i][j] remains zero. Otherwise, the value of dp[i][j] is the sum of the number of ways to take i cupcakes using the first j+1 colors of frosting, and the number of ways to take i - dij cupcakes using the first j+1 colors of frosting.

