\begin{align*}
f(1) &= 2^1 \\
f(2^1) &= 2^{(2^1)} \\
f(2^{2^1}) &= 2^{(2^{(2^1)})} \\
f(2^{2^{2^1}}) &= 2^{(2^{(2^{(2^1)})})}
\end{align*}
After making multiple function calls, we've arrived at an expression represented by $2^{((2^{(2^{(2^1)})})}$.
The last part of the problem is to compute $\sqrt{f(f(f(f(1))))}.$ Notice that applying the function twice will essentially be squaring the result:
